# Project structure

```
src/backend/{llm-orchestrator,external-api-service,external-channel-service,call-records-service,identity-service,ops-service}  — one service per folder
src/frontend/{admin-panel,super-admin-panel,driver-web,agents-playground,...}     — one app per folder
src/e2e/                                                         — cross-service scripts only
```

## Rules

- **One concern per file** — tools, routes, services, prompts in separate modules
- **No duplicate logic** — shared code lives once (e.g. `voicebot/prompts/`, `processors/trip_format.py`)
- **Service boundaries** — llm-orchestrator calls external-api-service via HTTP; no direct DB access from Python. Super Admin UI calls **ops-service** only (ops proxies call-records-service and tails log files).
- **Lang split** — `voicebot/vn/` and `voicebot/en/` mirror each other; shared logic in `processors/`, `prompts/`, `services/`
- **Requirements/docs** — product specs in `llm-orchestrator/requirements/`, not mixed into code
- **Service packages** — `services/<domain>/` (folder + public `index`/`__init__`). Compose adapters; no DI container. See `.cursor/rules/service-layer.mdc`.

## File naming

| Layer | Python | TypeScript |
|-------|--------|------------|
| HTTP routes | — | `routes/*.ts` |
| Business logic | `services/<name>/` | `services/<name>/` (legacy: `*Service.ts`) |
| Agent tools | `voicebot/{lang}/tools/*.py` | — |
| Prompts | `voicebot/prompts/`, `system_instructions.py` | — |
